  "body": "## Problem\n\n2D Contour tabs are narrower than the \"Tab width\" that the user sets. At its narrowest section (the centre line of the cut channel) the tab is `tab_width - tool diameter` wide. When the tab width is equal to or less than the tool diameter, no tab stays. The part comes free during the last levels, and no message tells the user.\n\n## Cause\n\n`Ring::tab_keeps` and `Ring::tab_keeps_from_start` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/ring.rs`) measure the tab window on the tool-centre ring. At each end of that window the cutter disc removes `D/2` more material along the centre line of the channel. The bridge is thus `tab_width` wide at the part wall, but only `tab_width - D` wide at the channel centre line.\n\nExample: a 6 mm end mill and a tab width of 5 mm. The window on the centre path is 5 mm long. On the channel centre line the cutter removes 3 mm on each side past the window ends. The two cuts overlap by 1 mm (5 - 6 = -1 mm), so the bridge is cut through.\n\n## Expected result\n\nThe tab width is the smallest width of the bridge that stays. For this, the window on the centre ring must be `tab_width + D` long.\n\nIf a tab cannot stay (for example, the window with the tool diameter is longer than the tab spacing), refuse the operation by name. Do not cut the part free silently.\n\n## Related\n\n- #1565: Verify and the stock sim do not find a piece of stock that the program frees. Thus this defect is not found by verify either.\n\n## Proposed priority\n\n`P1` by the AGENTS.md table: wrong output that passes. A freed part can move into the cutter.\n\nI can make the fix and a test (shape-mask test of the bridge width) in a PR from my fork.\n",
